# Deny by default.
#
# This workspace holds two independent git repositories (MKTTool, MKTBrowser) alongside relay
# identity material — DPAPI-sealed operator domain keys and device private keys live in
# local-test-artifacts/ and relay-identity-backup-*/. An allowlist is the only safe shape here: a
# denylist would need updating every time a new kind of secret appears beside it, and the cost of
# missing one is publishing an operator key.
#
# Tracked here: the cross-repo audit plans and reports, which belong to neither repository because
# they span both, and which otherwise exist only on one disk.
*

!.gitignore
!AGENTS.md
!CLAUDE.md
!plans/
!plans/**

# Re-deny inside the allowlisted plan tree. Last matching pattern wins.
#
# .codex-home-probe/ is a 2.5 MB copy of a Codex home directory captured while probing the
# orchestrator runner: installation id, goals/logs/memories SQLite databases, and vendored system
# skills. Machine state, not plan material.
plans/**/.codex-home-probe/
#
# Raw restore-verification receipts carry production schema field names and token-bearing record
# structures. Only the sanitized receipt belongs in Git — see
# plans/260829-2125-internal-product-readiness/reports/restore-verify-receipt-redaction.md
plans/**/restore-verify-*.json
